  <h2>What’s the most popular Passoa cocktail?</h2>
  <figure>
    <img src={media('/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/pornstar-martini-cocktail-1.jpg')} width="500" height="666" alt="Pornstar Martini topped with half a passion fruit, beside a bottle of Bollinger and a shot of champagne" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  </figure>
  <p>The most popular cocktail that uses Passoa right now has to be the <a href="/cocktails/pornstar-martini/">Pornstar Martini</a>, or Passion Fruit Martini, depending on where you go and how family-friendly the venue is.</p>
  <p>It combines Passoa with luxurious vanilla vodka, passion fruit juice and lime juice to create something truly remarkable.</p>

  <h2>What equipment you’ll need to make Passoa cocktails</h2>
  <p>To make these delicious Passoa cocktails, you’re going to need the following cocktail equipment.</p>

  <h3>A cocktail shaker</h3>
  <p><a href="/cocktail-equipment/">Cocktail shakers improve the taste of cocktails</a>. It’s a fact. There’s a reason the famous British spy James Bond says <strong><em>“shaken, not stirred”</em></strong>, and that reason is: it tastes better.</p>
  <p>If you don’t already have a <a href="/cocktail-equipment/#cocktail-shaker">cocktail shaker set</a>, you might want to check out <a href="/cocktail-sets/">our detailed cocktail shaker comparison</a>. But to cut a long story short, here’s the one we recommend:</p>
  <aside class="pick" aria-label="Our cocktail shaker pick">
